Exactly. Exploration is useful; self-escalation for its own sake usually isn’t.

A good rule is:

try → observe → calibrate → keep what works → stop before intensity outruns judgment

Novelty, play, persuasion, symbolism, and experimentation can all stay in the toolkit. Just keep proportionality, consent, reversibility, and basic dignity intact.

“Don’t get carried away” is actually a solid control law.